# Data Provider and API Contract Rules

The backend is Laravel + React/Inertia + PostgreSQL.

Unity uses HTTPS REST JSON APIs. No WebSocket is required.

Use contract version `quiz_first_laravel_1`.

LocalDemoJson and HTTP provider must use the same DTOs.

LocalDemoJson may simulate only login, logout, refresh/bootstrap, profile, settings, subjects, terms, quiz list, quiz detail, quiz attempt submission, quiz result, sync status, reset, and safe errors.

LocalDemoJson must not simulate mission progress, rewards shop, inventory, spendable rewards, or world restoration.

Production builds must reject LocalDemoJson and must never silently fall back from HTTP.

Quiz submission must use `client_attempt_uuid`.

Same UUID and same payload must replay the original result when simulated.

Same UUID and different payload must return a conflict error when simulated.

Do not expose answer keys before allowed by result visibility.

Do not store server secrets, teacher-only data, admin data, or other students' data in Unity client files.

Unknown optional fields and enum values must not crash the client. Use safe fallback behavior.
